    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and all 3 of its tests pass. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner `email` support end-to-end: present-but-invalid \u2192 400, otherwise stored and returned lower-cased, and absent is accepted.\n\n**Schema / spec**\n- `openapi.yml`: added an optional `email` property (`type: string`, `format: email`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain an `email` field (and GET returns it via the existing MapStruct mapping).\n- Added an `email VARCHAR(255)`/`TEXT` column to the `owners` table in all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql`: converted the positional owner `INSERT`s to explicit column lists so the new nullable column doesn't break seed loading (h2/postgres already listed columns; mysql has no owner seed rows).\n\n**Domain**\n- `Owner` entity: added the `email` field with `@Column(name=\"email\")` plus getter/setter.\n\n**Function pipeline (OfficeFloor)**\n- New `OwnerEmail` helper: validates a non-blank email against a syntactic pattern, throwing `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (checked) when invalid, and lower-cases it in place; leaves an absent email untouched.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST `/api/owners`) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT `/api/owners/{ownerId}`) now call `OwnerEmail.normalize(...)`.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT path) now copies `email` onto the entity.\n- New `InvalidOwnerEmailException`, its `InvalidOwnerEmailExceptionHandler` (responds 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`), and the matching escalation YAML \u2014 mirroring the existing telephone handling.\n\nAll 3 acceptance tests (`coreLowercasesEmail`, `errorRejectsInvalidEmail`, `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
